msgid ""
"Submission-row basis: counts completed form submission rows. This is not a "
"unique visitor count; one visitor or session can submit more than once where"
" the form allows it."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1748
msgid "How many completed form submission rows were tracked."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1753
msgid ""
"Form-interaction basis: submissions divided by tracked form "
"views/interactions for the selected filters. It is not calculated from "
"unique Visitors or Sessions KPIs."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1754
msgid "Submission rows divided by tracked form views/interactions."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1758
msgid "Average Completion Time"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1759
msgid ""
"The average time visitors spend filling out a form from first interaction to"
" submission. Very long times may suggest confusing fields. Very short times "
"might indicate auto-fill usage."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1760
msgid "How long it takes on average for someone to fill out your form."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1764
msgid "Abandonments"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1765
msgid ""
"The number of times visitors started interacting with a form but left "
"without submitting. High abandonment indicates friction — check the Field "
"Analysis tab to see where users drop off."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1766
msgid "Visitors who started filling out the form but gave up."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1770
msgid "Form Activity Over Time"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1771
msgid ""
"Submission/interaction basis: visualizes daily form submission and "
"abandonment rows over the selected period, not unique visitors."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1772
msgid "A chart showing form activity day by day."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1776
#: opti-behavior/views/emails/report-email-html.php:913
msgid "Top Forms by Conversion"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1777
msgid ""
"Form-interaction basis: ranks forms by submissions divided by tracked form "
"views/interactions for each form."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1778
msgid "Which of your forms are the most successful."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1782
msgid "Recent Form Activity"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1783
msgid ""
"Shows tracked forms with form-view, submission, abandonment, and related "
"session metrics. Form counts are row/interactions-based; Sessions badges "
"count matching session rows."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1784
msgid "A list of all your forms and how they are performing."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1788
msgid "Field Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1789
msgid ""
"Analyzes each field in your form individually. See which fields cause the "
"most drop-offs, take the longest to fill, or have the highest error rates. "
"Use this to simplify your forms."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1790
msgid "Shows which form fields cause problems for visitors."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1794
msgid "Field Drop-off Funnel"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1795
msgid ""
"Visualizes how visitors progress through your form fields. Each step shows "
"how many visitors reached that field and the drop-off rate. Fields with high"
" drop-off need attention."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1796
msgid "Shows where visitors stop filling out your form."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1800
msgid "Field-Level Metrics"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1801
msgid ""
"Detailed metrics for each form field: time spent, interaction count, error "
"rate, refill rate, and blank rate. Identify problematic fields that need "
"redesigning or clearer labels."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1802
msgid "Detailed stats for every field in your form."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1807
msgid ""
"View individual visitor sessions that interacted with this form. See their "
"submission status, device, country, and watch their session recording to "
"understand their experience."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1808
msgid "Individual visits where someone used this form."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1812
msgid "Device Filter"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1813
msgid ""
"Filter form analytics by device type (Desktop, Mobile, Tablet). Compare how "
"forms perform across different devices to identify mobile-specific issues."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1814
msgid "Show data only for specific devices."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1819
msgid ""
"Filter by browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, etc.). Useful for identifying "
"browser-specific form rendering or validation issues."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1820
msgid "Show data only for specific browsers."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1825
msgid ""
"Filter form analytics by visitor country. Helps you understand geographic "
"patterns and whether localization affects form completion."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1826
msgid "Show data only for visitors from specific countries."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1831
msgid ""
"Filters form analytics rows by the visitor type attached to each matching "
"form submission/session. Filter option counts are submission-row based, not "
"unique visitors."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1832
msgid "Show matching form activity for new or returning visitor-type rows."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1836
msgid "Referrer Filter"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1837
msgid ""
"Filter by traffic source (Google, social media, direct, etc.). See which "
"traffic sources bring the most form conversions."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1838
msgid "Show data based on where visitors came from."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1857
msgid "What is A/B Testing?"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1858
msgid ""
"Split testing lets you show different versions of a page to different "
"visitors, then measure which version converts better."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1859
msgid "Compare two or more versions of a page to find which one works best."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1862
msgid "Create a New Test"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1863
msgid ""
"Start the test builder wizard to set up a new split test. Takes about 2 "
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1867
msgid "Active Tests"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1868
msgid ""
"Tests currently serving different variants to your visitors and collecting "
"conversion data."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1872
msgid "Draft Tests"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1873
msgid ""
"Tests you have configured but not yet launched. Drafts do not affect your "
"live site."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1877
msgid "Completed Tests"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1878
msgid ""
"Tests that have been stopped or have declared a winner. Results are "
"preserved for review."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1883
msgid ""
"The total number of times any variant was shown to a visitor across all your"
" tests."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1887
msgid "Filter by Status"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1888
msgid ""
"Show only tests in a specific status: Running, Draft, Paused, Completed, or "
"Archived."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1892
msgid "Filter by Test Type"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1893
msgid "Show only Page Split, Element, or WooCommerce tests."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1897
msgid "Search Tests"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1898
msgid "Search by test name to quickly find a specific experiment."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1902
msgid "Free Plan Limits"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1903
msgid ""
"The free plan allows up to 3 concurrent tests, 3 variants per test, and 1 "
"goal per test. Upgrade to Pro to remove all limits."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1910
msgid "Step 1 – Test Type"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1911
msgid ""
"Choose the kind of test you want to run. You can change this before "
"launching but not after."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1916
msgid ""
"Redirects visitors to entirely different page URLs. Each URL is a separate "
"variant. Great for testing completely new page designs."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1921
msgid ""
"Modifies specific elements (text, buttons, images) on the same URL using the"
" visual editor. Visitors never leave the original page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1925
msgid "WooCommerce Product Test"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1926
msgid ""
"Tests different product titles, prices, descriptions, or images on "
"WooCommerce product pages. Measures impact on add-to-cart and revenue."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1927
#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2031
#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2036
#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2056
msgid "Requires Pro."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1933
msgid "Step 2 – Target"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1934
msgid ""
"Set the page where the test runs and give your test a recognisable name."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1939
msgid ""
"A descriptive label for your own reference — e.g., \"Homepage Hero CTA "
"Test\". Not shown to visitors."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1944
msgid ""
"The URL of the page where visitors will be split into variants. Use the full"
" URL including https://."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1948
msgid "Target Page or Post"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1949
msgid ""
"Pick from your published pages, posts, or products. The test will run on the"
" selected content's URL."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1954
msgid ""
"Search and select the product whose page you want to A/B test. Changes will "
"affect the product display in each variant."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1958
msgid "Search Products"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1959
msgid ""
"Search by product name, SKU, or category to quickly find the product to "
"test."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1963
msgid "Filter by Category"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1964
msgid "Narrow the product list to a specific WooCommerce product category."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1971
msgid "Step 3 – Variants"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:1972
msgid ""
"Define the different versions you want to compare. You always need at least "
"one variant in addition to the original (Control)."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2001
msgid "Add Another Variant"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2002
msgid ""
"Add a new variant to test. The free plan supports up to 3 variants total "
"(including Control)."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2009
msgid "Step 4 – Goals"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2010
msgid ""
"A goal is the action you want visitors to take. The test will track how "
"often each variant achieves this goal."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2014
msgid "Page Visit Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2015
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor lands on a specific URL — e.g., a thank-"
"you page after purchase."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2019
msgid "Click Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2020
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor clicks any element matching a CSS selector"
" — e.g., a buy button or link."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2024
msgid "Form Submit Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2025
msgid "Count a conversion when a visitor submits a form on the page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2029
msgid "Scroll Depth Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2030
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor scrolls past a certain percentage of the "
"page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2034
msgid "Time on Page Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2035
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor spends at least a set amount of time on "
"the page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2039
msgid "Revenue Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2040
msgid ""
"Track the total revenue generated by visitors in each variant. Requires "
"WooCommerce and Pro."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2041
#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2046
#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2051
msgid "Requires Pro + WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2044
msgid "Add to Cart Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2045
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor adds a product to cart. Requires "
"WooCommerce and Pro."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2049
msgid "Purchase Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2050
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor completes a WooCommerce purchase. Requires"
" WooCommerce and Pro."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2054
msgid "Bounce Rate Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2055
msgid ""
"Count a conversion when a visitor stays on the page longer than a threshold "
"(or leaves before it). Requires Pro."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2074
msgid "Add Another Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2075
msgid ""
"Add a second (or more) goal to track multiple conversions simultaneously. "
"Free plan: 1 goal per test."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2082
msgid "Step 5 – Settings"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2083
msgid ""
"Configure statistical thresholds and traffic settings. The defaults are "
"suitable for most tests."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2088
msgid ""
"How certain the statistical model must be before declaring a winner. 95% "
"(recommended) means a 1-in-20 chance of a false positive. Higher = fewer "
"false positives, but needs more data."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2093
msgid ""
"What percentage of total page visitors will be enrolled in the test. Set "
"below 100% to run the test on a subset of your audience — useful to reduce "
"risk."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2098
msgid ""
"The test will not declare significance until each variant has received at "
"least this many impressions. Prevents premature winners."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2102
msgid "Minimum Duration"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2103
msgid ""
"The test will run for at least this many days, even if statistical "
"significance is reached sooner. Guards against day-of-week effects."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2107
msgid "Save as Draft"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2108
msgid ""
"Save your current configuration without launching. You can return to edit or"
" launch later."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2112
msgid "Launch the Test"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2113
msgid ""
"Activate the test. Visitors will immediately start seeing different "
"variants. Make sure all settings are correct first."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2120
msgid "Step 6 – Review & Launch"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2121
msgid ""
"A summary of every setting you configured. Review carefully — you cannot "
"change the test type or target URL after launching."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2153
msgid "Test Results"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2154
msgid ""
"This page shows live performance data for your A/B test. Data updates as "
"visitors interact with your variants."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2159
msgid "This test is live and actively splitting traffic between variants."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2164
msgid ""
"This test is temporarily suspended. Traffic is no longer split, but no data "
"is lost."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2169
msgid "This test has finished. A winner may have been declared."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2173
msgid "Pause the Test"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2174
msgid ""
"Temporarily stop splitting traffic. All visitors see the Control until the "
"test is resumed. Data is preserved."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2178
msgid "Resume the Test"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2179
msgid ""
"Restart traffic splitting from where it was paused. Data collection "
"continues."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2183
msgid "Stop the Test"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2184
msgid ""
"Permanently end the test. This cannot be undone. All data collected so far "
"is preserved."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2189
msgid ""
"The total number of unique visitor impressions across all variants combined "
"since the test started."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2194
msgid ""
"How long the test has been running in days. Longer tests produce more "
"reliable results."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2198
msgid "Best Conversion Rate"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2199
msgid ""
"The highest conversion rate achieved by any single variant. Compare variants"
" to find your winner."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2203
msgid "Statistical Confidence"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2204
msgid ""
"How certain the statistical model is that the observed difference between "
"variants is real, not due to random chance. Aim for 95% or higher."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2208
msgid "Select a Goal"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2209
msgid ""
"Choose which goal's conversion data to display. Each goal has its own set of"
" variant charts."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2214
msgid ""
"The specific settings for the currently selected goal — e.g., the target URL"
" or CSS selector used to detect conversions."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2218
msgid "Statistical Significance Gauge"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2219
msgid ""
"The arc fills as more data is collected. Reaching 95% means results are "
"statistically significant and reliable enough to act on."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2223
msgid "Confidence Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2224
msgid ""
"The threshold configured in Step 5. The test will not auto-declare a winner "
"below this level."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2239
msgid ""
"The raw number of visitors who completed the goal while seeing this variant."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2254
msgid ""
"Stop the test and record the variant with the highest conversion rate as the"
" winner."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2259
msgid ""
"Route 100% of traffic to this variant permanently. For Element tests, the "
"variant's DOM changes are saved to the page. This action cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2263
msgid "Conversion Rate Chart"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2264
msgid ""
"Shows how each variant's conversion rate evolved over the test's duration. "
"Converging lines indicate an inconclusive test; diverging lines point to a "
"clear winner."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2268
msgid "No Data Yet"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2269
msgid ""
"No conversions have been recorded yet. Make sure the goal is set up "
"correctly and that real visitors have seen the variants."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2274
msgid ""
"The test has collected enough data to declare a statistically significant "
"winner with high confidence."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2279
msgid ""
"Officially end the test and record the variant with the highest conversion "
"rate as the winner. The test status changes to Completed."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2283
msgid "Apply Winner Permanently"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2284
msgid ""
"Overwrite the original page with the winning variant's content. Only "
"available for Element and WooCommerce test types."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2289
msgid ""
"Stop the permanent winner change and return the test to Completed. The "
"winner and historical data remain available."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2311
msgid "What is this signal?"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2312
msgid ""
"Smart Insights compares this page, form, funnel, or audience against your "
"own site baseline for the selected period. A card appears when the "
"difference is large enough and is measured on enough sessions to be trusted."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2313
msgid "A behavior pattern that stands out from your normal numbers."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2318
msgid "Bounce rate alert"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2319
msgid ""
"Measures the share of sessions on a page that end without a second page "
"view. It triggers when a page with enough traffic bounces clearly more than "
"your site baseline for the same period."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2320
msgid "Too many visitors leave this page after seeing only that page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2323
msgid "Mobile bounce warning"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2324
msgid ""
"Compares the bounce rate of mobile sessions against desktop sessions on the "
"same page. It triggers when mobile bounces noticeably more, which usually "
"points at layout, speed, or tap-target problems on small screens."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2325
msgid "Phone visitors leave much faster than desktop visitors."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2328
msgid "High exit rate page"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2329
msgid ""
"Measures how often a page is the last one seen in a session. Unlike bounce "
"rate it also counts visitors who arrived from another page, so it flags "
"pages where journeys stop rather than pages where they start badly."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2330
msgid "Visitors reach this page and then stop browsing."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2333
msgid "High traffic, low engagement"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2334
msgid ""
"Combines traffic volume with engagement signals such as time on page, scroll"
" depth, and interactions. It triggers when a page receives a lot of visits "
"but visitors do very little once they arrive."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2335
msgid "A popular page that visitors barely engage with."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2338
msgid "Low scroll depth"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2339
msgid ""
"Measures how far down a page visitors scroll on average. It triggers on "
"pages with meaningful traffic where most visitors never reach the lower part"
" of the page, so content or calls to action placed there are rarely seen."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2340
msgid "Most visitors never scroll far enough to see the bottom of this page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2343
msgid "Traffic spike"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2344
msgid ""
"Compares session volume for the current period against the previous one. It "
"triggers when traffic rises sharply. This is an observation, not a problem: "
"it is there so you can check whether the extra traffic behaves like your "
"usual audience."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2345
msgid "Traffic jumped compared with the period before."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2350
msgid "Quick exit pattern"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2351
msgid ""
"Looks at how quickly sessions end after landing. It triggers when an unusual"
" share of visitors leave within the first seconds, before any real reading "
"or interaction can happen."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2352
msgid "Visitors leave within seconds of arriving."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2355
msgid "Engagement decay"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2356
msgid ""
"Compares current engagement (time, scroll, interactions) against the same "
"page in the previous period. It triggers when engagement drops over time "
"rather than being low all along, which usually follows a content, layout, or"
" speed change."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2357
msgid "This page used to hold attention better than it does now."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2360
msgid "Visitor confusion"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2361
msgid ""
"Combines hesitation signals such as erratic scrolling, back-and-forth "
"navigation, and repeated clicking on the same area. It triggers when many "
"sessions show the behavior of people who cannot find what they came for."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2362
msgid "Visitors act lost on this page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2365
msgid "Dead and rage clicks"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2366
msgid ""
"Dead clicks are clicks on something that does nothing. Rage clicks are "
"several fast clicks on the same spot. The signal triggers when either "
"happens often enough on one element to indicate a broken or misleading "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2367
msgid "Visitors click something that does not react."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2370
msgid "Session recording opportunity"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2371
msgid ""
"Fires when a measured problem has recordings available that show the "
"behavior directly. It does not detect a new issue: it tells you that "
"watching a few real sessions is the fastest way to understand this one."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2372
msgid "Recordings exist that show this problem happening."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2375
msgid "A/B test opportunity"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2376
msgid ""
"Fires on pages where traffic is high enough for a split test to reach a "
"usable result, and where a measured weakness gives you something concrete to"
" test. It suggests validating a fix rather than shipping it blind."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2377
msgid "This page has enough traffic to test a change properly."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2382
msgid "Low CTA performance"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2383
msgid ""
"Measures how many visitors who saw a call to action actually clicked it. It "
"triggers when the click rate is clearly below what comparable elements on "
"your site achieve, after enough impressions to be reliable."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2384
msgid "People see this button or link but do not click it."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2387
msgid "Poor conversion rate"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2388
msgid ""
"Compares the conversion rate of a page or flow against your site baseline. "
"It triggers when the rate stays below that baseline over enough sessions "
"that the gap is unlikely to be noise."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2389
msgid "Traffic arrives but few visitors complete the goal."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2392
msgid "Conversion drop"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2393
msgid ""
"Compares the current conversion rate against the previous period for the "
"same scope. It triggers on a sudden fall, which usually means something "
"changed recently: a deploy, a price, a tracking break, or a traffic mix "
"shift."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2394
msgid "Conversions fell compared with the period before."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2397
msgid "Traffic spike without conversion"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2398
msgid ""
"Triggers when session volume rises sharply while conversions stay flat. The "
"extra visitors behave differently from your usual audience, which typically "
"points at a low-intent source, a campaign mismatch, or bot-like traffic."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2399
msgid "More visitors arrived, but the extra visitors do not convert."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2404
msgid "Mobile friction"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2405
msgid ""
"Compares mobile sessions against desktop sessions on the same page using "
"engagement, errors, and interaction signals. It triggers when the mobile "
"experience is measurably worse, not merely different."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2406
msgid "The mobile version of this page performs worse than desktop."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2409
msgid "Mobile CTA gap"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2410
msgid ""
"Compares the click rate of the same call to action on mobile and on desktop."
" It triggers when mobile clicks clearly lag, which usually means the element"
" is hidden below the fold, too small to tap, or covered by a sticky bar."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2411
msgid "The same button gets clicked far less on phones."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2416
msgid "Low quality traffic source"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2417
msgid ""
"Groups sessions by source and compares their engagement and conversion "
"against your site average. It triggers when one source sends enough sessions"
" to be judged and those sessions consistently underperform."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2418
msgid "One traffic source brings visitors who do not engage."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2421
msgid "Campaign and page mismatch"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2422
msgid ""
"Compares what a campaign promises with how its visitors behave on the "
"landing page. It triggers when campaign traffic bounces or disengages much "
"faster than other traffic on the same page, which points at a promise the "
"page does not keep."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2423
msgid "Campaign visitors do not find what the ad led them to expect."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2426
msgid "Segment anomaly"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2427
msgid ""
"Splits sessions by device, browser, country, source, and campaign and looks "
"for one group that behaves very differently from the rest. It triggers only "
"when the group is large enough for the difference to be statistically "
"meaningful."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2428
msgid "One audience group behaves very differently from everyone else."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2431
msgid "Returning visitor opportunity"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2432
msgid ""
"Compares returning visitors with first-time visitors. It triggers when "
"returning visitors show clearly stronger intent than the experience "
"currently rewards, so a targeted offer or shortcut is likely to pay off."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2433
msgid "Your returning visitors are worth more than the page treats them."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2439
msgid ""
"Follows visitors from one funnel step to the next. It triggers when one step"
" loses a much larger share of visitors than the steps around it, which "
"isolates where the journey breaks."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2440
msgid "One step in the funnel loses far more visitors than the others."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2443
msgid "Product page to cart drop-off"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2444
msgid ""
"Measures how many product page visitors add an item to the cart. It triggers"
" when that share falls clearly below your store baseline, which usually "
"points at price, stock, shipping information, or a weak add-to-cart action."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2445
msgid "Visitors view the product but do not add it to the cart."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2448
msgid "Product page engagement issue"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2449
msgid ""
"Looks at time, scroll, and interactions on product pages. It triggers when "
"visitors do not reach the information that normally drives a purchase "
"decision, such as images, description, or reviews."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2450
msgid "Shoppers do not engage with this product page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2453
msgid "Cart to checkout drop-off"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2454
msgid ""
"Measures how many visitors with a filled cart actually start checkout. It "
"triggers when that share is unusually low, which typically points at "
"unexpected costs, an account requirement, or an unclear checkout entry "
"point."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2455
msgid "Carts are filled but checkout is never started."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2458
msgid "Checkout to purchase drop-off"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2459
msgid ""
"Measures how many visitors who start checkout finish the order. It triggers "
"when the completion share is clearly below baseline, which is the most "
"expensive place on the site to lose someone."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2460
msgid "Checkout is started but the order is not completed."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2463
msgid "Checkout friction"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2464
msgid ""
"Combines errors, hesitation, field corrections, and time spent inside the "
"checkout steps. It triggers when the checkout is measurably harder to "
"complete than the rest of the journey, and points at the step responsible."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2465
msgid "Something inside checkout is slowing buyers down."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2471
msgid ""
"Compares how many visitors start a form against how many submit it. It "
"triggers when a form with enough starts is abandoned much more often than "
"your other forms."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2472
msgid "Visitors begin this form but never send it."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2475
msgid "Form error friction"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2476
msgid ""
"Counts validation errors raised while a form is being filled. It triggers "
"when errors are frequent enough to be a design problem rather than normal "
"typing mistakes, for example an unclear format rule."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2477
msgid "This form rejects visitors too often before they can submit."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2480
msgid "Field level friction"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2481
msgid ""
"Narrows form problems down to a single field using time spent, corrections, "
"re-entries, and abandonment at that field. It triggers when one field is "
"measurably harder than the rest of the form."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2482
msgid "One specific field is where people give up."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2485
msgid "Error impact on conversion"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2486
msgid ""
"Compares sessions that hit a JavaScript error with sessions that did not, on"
" the same page. It triggers when the error group converts or engages clearly"
" worse, which turns a technical error into a measured business cost."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2487
msgid "Sessions that hit this error perform worse than clean sessions."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2511
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:779
msgid "Business impact"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2512
msgid ""
"Translates the signal into what it costs you: how many sessions or visitors "
"are affected, and where available the estimated lost revenue. Figures are "
"estimates based on your own measured rates for the selected period, not "
"predictions."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2513
msgid "What this problem is worth in visitors or money."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2516
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:736
msgid "Diagnosis"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2517
msgid ""
"The interpretation of the measured numbers: what the data most likely means "
"and why it matters for your site. It explains the finding; it does not add "
"new measurements."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2518
msgid "What the numbers most likely mean."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2521
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:737
msgid "Evidence"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2522
msgid ""
"The raw metrics behind the card: the measured value, the baseline it is "
"compared with, and the number of sessions the comparison rests on. If the "
"session count is small, treat the finding as directional."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2523
msgid "The actual numbers that triggered this insight."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2526
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:923
msgid "Evidence and proof"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2527
msgid ""
"Direct links to the recordings, heatmaps, form reports, or error entries "
"that show this behavior. Each link opens the matching report already "
"filtered to the page, period, and segment of this insight."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2528
msgid "Open the recordings and reports that prove this finding."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2531
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:927
msgid "Hypothesis and next experiment"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2532
msgid ""
"A testable explanation of the cause, plus the change worth trying and how to"
" measure it. Treat it as a starting point for an A/B test, not as a "
"confirmed cause."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2533
msgid "What to try next, and how to check whether it worked."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2536
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:1001
msgid "Experiment result"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2537
msgid ""
"The outcome of the test that was run for this insight: whether the metric "
"improved, stayed flat, or got worse after the change, measured against the "
"period before it."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2538
msgid "What happened after the change was applied."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2541
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:836
msgid "Where is the problem?"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2542
msgid ""
"Splits the affected sessions by device, browser, country, traffic source, "
"and campaign to show whether one audience carries the problem or whether it "
"is spread evenly. If it is spread evenly, the page itself is the cause, not "
"a segment."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2543
msgid "Which audience group actually has this problem."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2546
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:871
msgid "Segment health"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2547
msgid ""
"One dot per audience group. Red means the group carries the problem, amber "
"means it is worth watching, green means it behaves normally, and gray means "
"too few sessions were measured to judge it. The counter shows how many "
"groups cleared the data floor."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2548
msgid ""
"Red carries the problem, amber is borderline, green is fine, gray is not "
"measurable."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2551
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:880
msgid "Segments that differ most"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2552
msgid ""
"Each card compares one audience group with everyone else on the same metric."
" The paired bars show both values, the arrow shows whether the group got "
"better or worse between the first and second half of the period, and the "
"small chart shows the daily values. Cards marked \"Combined\" describe a "
"pair such as one browser on one country, detected because neither part alone"
" explained the problem. Clicking a card re-scopes the chart and the report "
"links to that group."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2553
msgid "One card per audience group, compared against everyone else."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2556
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:897
msgid "Did the audience change?"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2557
msgid ""
"Compares the share each country, source, or device holds this period against"
" the previous one. A large shift means your audience composition changed, so"
" a metric can move without any page changing. Shown only when the shift is "
"big enough and measured on enough sessions."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2558
msgid "Whether the metric moved because your audience changed, not the page."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2562
msgid ""
"The scope of the finding: the period analyzed, the page or entity involved, "
"the confidence level, and how often this insight has recurred. Read it "
"before acting so you know exactly what the numbers cover."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2563
msgid "What period, page, and reliability this insight covers."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2566
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:771
msgid "Next action"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2567
msgid ""
"The single highest-value step for this insight, chosen from the full "
"recommendation list. Start here when you only have time for one change."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2568
msgid "The one thing to do first."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2571
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:1019
msgid "Related reports"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2572
msgid ""
"Shortcuts into the reports that hold the underlying data: heatmaps, "
"recordings, funnels, forms, and traffic reports. Each link carries the page,"
" period, and segment of this insight, so you land on the matching view "
"instead of the report home."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2573
msgid "Open the full reports behind this insight."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2576
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:770
msgid "Recommended actions"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2577
msgid ""
"Concrete changes matched to this signal type, ordered by expected effect. "
"They are suggestions based on common causes for this pattern, so check them "
"against what you know about the page before applying one."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2578
msgid "Changes worth trying, most promising first."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2581
#: opti-behavior/includes/trait-opti-behavior-assets.php:773
msgid "Likely causes"
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2582
msgid ""
"The explanations that most often produce this pattern. Causes marked as "
"measured were confirmed against your own data; the others are candidates to "
"rule out one by one."
msgstr ""

#: opti-behavior/includes/tooltip-helper.php:2583
msgid "What usually causes a pattern like this."
msgstr ""

